## What changed

**`src/slugify.ts`** — added two steps before the existing lowercase/dash logic:

```ts
export function slugify(text: string): string {
  return text
    .normalize('NFD')
    .replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g, '')
    .toLowerCase()
    .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')
    .replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '')
}
```

NFD decomposition splits each accented Latin letter into its base letter plus a combining diacritical mark; the `\u0300-\u036f` range strips those combining marks, so `Crème Brûlée` becomes `creme-brulee`. The existing rules (one dash per run of non-letter/digit, leading/trailing dashes dropped, empty result for punctuation-only input) were already handled by the original two regexes.

**`src/slugify.test.ts`** — kept the original test and added four covering the requested behaviors:
- accented Latin letters reduced (`Crème Brûlée`, `ÀÉÎÕÜ`, `piñata café`)
- runs of non-letter/digit collapsed to one dash (`Hello   World`, `a!!b`, `Hello, World!`, `version_1.2`)
- leading/trailing dashes dropped (`  Hello World  `, `-Hello World-`, `!!Hello!!`)
- empty / punctuation-only returns `''` (`''`, `'!!!'`, `' - - '`, `'...?!'`)

