## Decisions the plan didn't spell out

The spec says "anything that is not a letter or a digit become one dash," but I kept the original ASCII rule `[^a-z0-9]` rather than switching to Unicode `\p{L}`/`\p{N}`: the slug is documented as URL-safe ASCII (`a-z0-9`), and treating e.g. Cyrillic as a "letter" to keep would produce non-URL-safe output and contradicts the existing doc comment. So non-Latin letters still become dashes; only Latin accents are reduced, which is exactly what the concrete example requires. Committed as `9ee8dca`.

